# Theme role sections (Oct 2026)

Authors edit colours on **Themes**; each role needs a one-line “where it applies,” not just the key name.

## Source of truth

- [`editor/src/model/themeRoles.ts`](editor/src/model/themeRoles.ts) — `THEME_ROLE_SECTIONS` (Chrome, Surfaces, Ink, Accents, Keys, Status, Overlays) + `PASTELS_INTRO`.
- [`ThemesView.vue`](editor/src/components/ThemesView.vue) — groups pickers from that catalogue; preview must demonstrate the roles.

## Preview must show

- Tile header line: `--rc-accent-soft` (off) / pastel (on) — not `card_header`
- Active nav: `--rc-ink` on `--rc-nav-on` (match live `ScreenRenderer.navButton`)
- Home strip: `home` / `home_strip` / `ink_dark`
- Status/keys: warn / danger / `key_on` samples; scrim corner optional
- Band captions under preview: Header / Cards / Nav

## Gotchas

- `ok` is picker-only today (no player `Role.OK` path) — blurb must say so.
- `key_on_ink` ≠ nav ink; nav stays `ink` on teal.
- When adding a Kotlin `Role`, add a section entry + CSS var via `themeVars` (`role_key` → `--rc-role-key`).
